cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Towards Vision Zero: the predictability ceiling for traffic
  accident severity in Quebec SAAQ collision data
message: Please cite this repository if you use it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Freiberg
    given-names: Tristan
repository-code: https://github.com/tmfreiberg/towards-vision-zero
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An investigation into how much the features recorded on Quebec
  police accident reports can tell us about collision severity.
  The analysis estimates an upper bound on achievable
  classification accuracy from the empirical label distribution
  within identical feature vectors, and a lower bound on error
  from mutual information via Fano's inequality, and argues that
  the resulting ceiling is a property of the data rather than of
  the model class or the quantity of training data.
keywords:
  - road safety
  - Vision Zero
  - Bayes error rate
  - calibration
  - SAAQ
references:
  - type: data
    title: Rapports d'accident
    authors:
      - name: Société de l'assurance automobile du Québec
        alias: SAAQ
    year: 2017
    url: https://www.donneesquebec.ca/recherche/dataset/rapports-d-accident
    notes: >-
      SOCIÉTÉ DE L'ASSURANCE AUTOMOBILE DU QUÉBEC (SAAQ). Rapports d'accident,
      [Jeu de données], dans Données Québec, 2017, mis à jour le 18 décembre
      2023. https://www.donneesquebec.ca/recherche/dataset/rapports-d-accident,
      (consulté le 13 mars 2024).

      Données issues des rapports d'accident remplis par les policiers, incluant
      notamment le moment, la gravité de l'accident de même que le type des
      véhicules impliqués.
